  "id": "ideomotor-theory",
  "term": "ideomotor theory",
  "definition": "Ideomotor theory is the view that voluntary action is guided by anticipating its sensory consequences. In this account, people learn links between movements and their effects, and later the expected effect can help bring about or select the associated action.",
  "field": "learning",
